-- title:
--   Remark 3.22: Semibounded coadjoint orbit through a central functional
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   In the faithful admissible structural setting, extend $f\in\mathfrak z^*$ to $F=f\circ p_z$ on $\mathfrak g$. This functional is fixed by inner exponentials from $\mathfrak l$, and
--
--   $$\mathcal O_F=\{F\circ e^{\operatorname{ad}v}:v\in V\},\qquad\mathcal O_F(x)=F(H_x^z(V)).$$
--
--   Its semibounded domain, defined by existence of a real lower bound on $\mathcal O_F(x)$, equals $\{x:F\text{ is bounded below on }\operatorname{co}_z(x)\}$. For $x_V=0$, membership in this domain is equivalent to $F(c)\ge0$ for every $c\in C_{x,z}$. No potentially unbounded real infimum is used.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 16, Remark 3.22: Semibounded coadjoint orbit through a central functional

